#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128941 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129130 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61bd0b4f-165c-5f31-b4ec-e0eff7e758e1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis Using a Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "76ff3ea8-e07c-5dba-a9af-a4f68b03fadb" :question/math-academy-id "e-5516" :question/problem "![](images/32/32b9b4bef130167d1da59e89933dea01a699ca4308decf54403f62ffb582ec20.svg)\n\nConsider the matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}}$ of a linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with respect to the basis $\\mathcal{B}$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix $P_{\\small \\mathcal{B} \\to \\mathcal{C}}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the bases $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C}$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{C}} = P_{\\small{\\mathcal{B}}\\to{\\mathcal{C}}} \\cdot [\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}} \\cdot P_{\\small{\\mathcal{B}}\\to{\\mathcal{C}}}^{-1}\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere $P_{\\small{\\mathcal{B}}\\to{\\mathcal{C}}}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{B}$ to $\\mathcal{C}.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{C}}.$ First, we compute the inverse of $P_{\\small{\\mathcal{B}}\\to{\\mathcal{C}}} \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 1-0\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C} \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -7 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -10 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128942 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129131 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "969220db-a686-511b-b33a-0b4f6ab66b1a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to the Standard Basis"}] :question/id #uuid "4b287ac7-7569-59bc-a319-0e62996083bc" :question/math-academy-id "e-5517" :question/problem "![](images/6d/6dea9ab921904f09ef76230fe87194b745f4f06eb9cfbbbbda0b3bd44722fc93.svg)\n\nConsider the basis $\\mathcal{B}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ and the matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}}$ of a linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with respect to this basis. Find the matrix of $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the standard basis $\\mathcal{S}.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}$ and standard basis $\\mathcal{S}$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/db/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{S}} = P_{\\small{\\mathcal{B}}\\to{\\mathcal{S}}} \\cdot [\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}} \\cdot P_{\\small{\\mathcal{B}}\\to{\\mathcal{S}}}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{B}$ to $\\mathcal{S}$ is\n\n![](images/01/01d05455345f8ec71e58f613d3bcf54c41f4ff196766c728871e54050f590fba.svg)\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of $P_{\\small{\\mathcal{B}}\\to{\\mathcal{S}}} \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 3-(-7)\\cdot (-2)}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the standard basis $\\mathcal{S} \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 13 \\\\ 3 & -9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 11 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128973 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129155 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86028fae-a119-5194-975d-a6d9fad6faf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Given Basis"}] :question/id #uuid "5e4b6303-8ec5-5ba6-ba1d-3b28ff8924b1" :question/math-academy-id "e-5897" :question/problem "![](images/4e/4ef9218607e5b3285d98967ec7cf44627ece6ecc5918f702fded329b1fe8ee4d.svg)\n\nConsider the bases $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2,$ and the matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}}$ of a linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with respect to the basis $\\mathcal{B}$, shown above. Find the matrix of $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the bases $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C}$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{C}} = P_{\\small{\\mathcal{B}}\\to{\\mathcal{C}}} \\cdot [\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}} \\cdot P_{\\small{\\mathcal{B}}\\to{\\mathcal{C}}}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere $P_{\\small{\\mathcal{B}}\\to{\\mathcal{C}}}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{B}$ to $\\mathcal{C}.$\n\nFirst, let's denote the vectors of $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C}$ as $\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1,\\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$ and $\\{ \\mathbf{c}_1,\\mathbf{c}_2 \\}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{B}$ to $\\mathcal{C}$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of vectors from $\\mathcal{B}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of $\\mathbf{b}_1$ and $\\mathbf{b}_2$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}.$ To do this, we consider the matrix\n\n![](images/26/26210267b80b50c4296225ac67237767cb326f2863fbfeba4cbdeb3f256ef62e.svg)\n\nWe reduce $M$ using Gaussian elimination until we get the identity matrix on the left. By doing this, we obtain the required change-of-coordinates matrix on the right.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n![](images/97/97450c835af63c4489b848a69986d5b496af1bf983355c65021aca3384826ca7.svg)\n\nNow, we compute the inverse of $P_{\\small{\\mathcal{B}}\\to{\\mathcal{C}}} \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 1-0\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can compute the matrix of $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C} \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129032 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "434a82c2-7964-525a-85b9-eb17fa7b5b26" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connections Between Matrices of a Linear Transformation Relative to Different Bases"}] :question/id #uuid "c269a1d0-a47c-5f5c-96d8-4da2ecd35a48" :question/math-academy-id "e-8563" :question/problem "Let $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}}$ and $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{C}}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the bases $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C},$ respectively. If $P_{\\small \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{B}}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $\\mathcal{C}$ to basis $\\mathcal{B},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}} = P_{\\small \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{B}} \\cdot [\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{C}}\\cdot P_{\\small \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{B}}^{-1}$\n\nII. $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{C}} = P_{\\small \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{B}}^{-1} \\cdot [\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}} \\cdot P_{\\small \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{B}}$\n\nIII. $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{C}} = P_{\\small \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{B}} \\cdot [\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}} \\cdot P_{\\small \\mathcal{B} \\to \\mathcal{C}}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the bases $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C}$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/2e/2e82c232614bec8a98f079ea56d7913ee13e7b457e33e418198278d2e369fc5c.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{C}} = P_{\\small \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{B}}^{-1} \\cdot [\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}} \\cdot P_{\\small \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{B}},\n$$\n\nwhere $P_{\\small \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{B}}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{C}$ to $\\mathcal{B}.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}} = P_{\\small \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{B}} \\cdot [\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{C}} \\cdot P_{\\small \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{B}}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272063 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "434a82c2-7964-525a-85b9-eb17fa7b5b26" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connections Between Matrices of a Linear Transformation Relative to Different Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de51a0dc-dd2e-51c5-bdf6-35f0d167a4af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449550} {:answer/id #uuid "3074d86e-e8f4-59b8-b9ef-b9acd04d1e72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de51a0dc-dd2e-51c5-bdf6-35f0d167a4af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449550} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b489027-47a6-5418-b1a4-ae90726f7d12" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450729} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5973a2ab-b2dd-592e-a584-1a43d4c02adf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449552} {:answer/id #uuid "475f048c-5791-5804-8edc-299acd62ba0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "475f048c-5791-5804-8edc-299acd62ba0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449553} :answer-field/id #uuid "9997d045-331c-54ca-b718-1546606cd597" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450730} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61266a01-b00a-5764-85eb-7849d7f3d7c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449554} {:answer/id #uuid "8422f214-fd53-5e1a-8fa7-538645d77eaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61266a01-b00a-5764-85eb-7849d7f3d7c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449554} :answer-field/id #uuid "85ff507d-5d08-5b56-a407-069075198e07" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf5001e6-d49e-526a-bbd2-b37f328e04e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-140361" :question/problem "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $B$ to basis $C,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$\n- **II.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$\n- **III.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388702 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129130 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61bd0b4f-165c-5f31-b4ec-e0eff7e758e1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis Using a Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39af9a4f-5bb0-5f67-b99e-b356fdeef13f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}20 & -36 \\\\ 14 & -25\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388704} {:answer/id #uuid "24019f33-d58e-5c2e-9bc0-2466a9447e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}20 & 36 \\\\ -25 & 14\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388705} {:answer/id #uuid "9eb9cc07-a4ed-5da6-b193-1c9894ee42b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}14 & -25 \\\\ 20 & -36\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388706} {:answer/id #uuid "1667976f-4e72-5f00-aab0-1b8c12345f8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}14 & -36 \\\\ 20 & -25\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388707} {:answer/id #uuid "d77416b1-f86b-5a81-a593-653abb91c3eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}25 & -36 \\\\ 14 & -20\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39af9a4f-5bb0-5f67-b99e-b356fdeef13f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}20 & -36 \\\\ 14 & -25\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388704} :answer-field/id #uuid "6811151d-cd95-5e12-aa34-9045fdbee48f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388703}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3fe32d4d-9284-57a0-89e5-58bdfd98337d" :question/math-academy-id "q-140454" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{C}.$ First, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}20 & -36 \\\\ 14 & -25\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480696 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129155 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86028fae-a119-5194-975d-a6d9fad6faf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Given Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18d7f229-8e52-50a6-aefb-b0cac4224645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -11 \\\\ 5 & -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480148} {:answer/id #uuid "22b7fe3f-06c5-50bf-974c-0d0810764de8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & -11 \\\\ 5 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480169} {:answer/id #uuid "2861eb9c-4514-5616-ba03-e8561c891eed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & -5 \\\\ 11 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480177} {:answer/id #uuid "4dcfa639-1ecc-55b1-9be1-e5cb4a37903f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 & -10 \\\\ 5 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480243} {:answer/id #uuid "50c0d953-a401-5471-947d-1ca57c74ec8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -5 \\\\ 10 & -11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480248}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22b7fe3f-06c5-50bf-974c-0d0810764de8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & -11 \\\\ 5 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480169} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8dc1988-bf2a-5231-bb4f-7e3b1ddd7888" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480626}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d84dee64-5460-51d7-b92e-0ebbf9e09851" :question/math-academy-id "q-140486" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,C=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the bases $B$ and $C$ of ${R}^{2},$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$, shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nFirst, let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ and $\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of vectors from $B$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ relative to the basis $C.$ To do this, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce $M$ using Gaussian elimination until we get the identity matrix on the left. By doing this, we obtain the required change-of-coordinates matrix on the right.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot (-1)-3\\cdot (-2)}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}17 & -9 \\\\ 10 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & -11 \\\\ 5 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375096 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129130 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61bd0b4f-165c-5f31-b4ec-e0eff7e758e1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis Using a Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "885275fa-0273-572d-b4ee-cd12300d505e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375098} {:answer/id #uuid "132ab69d-5679-5d1c-a1bc-aa2c6fcdc223" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375099} {:answer/id #uuid "a56f3d7b-6da1-52d8-acb8-91f8eaa8c91d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375100} {:answer/id #uuid "1bfad28a-987c-5e44-ae2b-d9da6d1bae04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375101} {:answer/id #uuid "86726a21-1a03-57e3-a79b-8a0905cbc6ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375102}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "885275fa-0273-572d-b4ee-cd12300d505e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375098} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ba2eb2d-11d8-5382-b28d-dd3142a80d57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375097}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "171fe4ce-730c-5fbe-99a6-2dbc5de82526" :question/math-academy-id "q-38357" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{C}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $C$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $B.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/2e/2e82c232614bec8a98f079ea56d7913ee13e7b457e33e418198278d2e369fc5c.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}.\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{B}.$ Solving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480637 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "434a82c2-7964-525a-85b9-eb17fa7b5b26" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connections Between Matrices of a Linear Transformation Relative to Different Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0318a7cd-6ed8-5929-a663-a34a94cdf12b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480117} {:answer/id #uuid "7532fabe-190b-58ef-a25b-c7b41103ed86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480301} {:answer/id #uuid "7a019de8-fdbb-5874-b9a3-954a21bd5b5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480311} {:answer/id #uuid "a361a1e4-9e64-5e97-880b-6eacdecce1af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480384} {:answer/id #uuid "f6f097ce-9807-535f-aa3b-32eb24813105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a019de8-fdbb-5874-b9a3-954a21bd5b5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480311} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd483cd6-8476-5430-add9-76a6040fadd1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480602}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "18c92889-12f7-533b-bf2f-74218efc0204" :question/math-academy-id "q-38361" :question/problem "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $C$ to basis $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $[T]_{B}=[T]_{C}^{-1}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}$\n\nII. $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}$\n\nIII. $[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/2e/2e82c232614bec8a98f079ea56d7913ee13e7b457e33e418198278d2e369fc5c.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129131 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "969220db-a686-511b-b33a-0b4f6ab66b1a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5669535f-e936-5808-865c-2ffa3ed1afbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324692} {:answer/id #uuid "686be3d1-f70d-534b-8c1d-122b77f7f1cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324843} {:answer/id #uuid "9c139bdc-ae5e-5940-826c-9936fe328b58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325293} {:answer/id #uuid "c6078509-e79b-537e-83f5-08de93f7a92f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325680} {:answer/id #uuid "e2c8c242-befa-55ad-8739-21acb222c6b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c139bdc-ae5e-5940-826c-9936fe328b58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325293} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8500d2d-7918-5e80-9683-a3d7c1f7ecbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326549}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3ef316a2-414a-55cd-b85b-e6597918be4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-38362" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to this basis. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the basis $B$ and standard basis $S$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/db/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326682 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129130 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61bd0b4f-165c-5f31-b4ec-e0eff7e758e1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis Using a Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a66c93a-af60-53aa-a747-1ca57d557a70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 34 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324193} {:answer/id #uuid "8e7b1556-61ad-5b7b-b55a-24309469ebf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}23 & -26 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325181} {:answer/id #uuid "b6c4df6c-f5d6-5a2a-93b7-7a763a5ccac4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -26 \\\\ -1 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325542} {:answer/id #uuid "b83ae89b-83e0-5034-b9a9-90ae55eaf725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 16 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325552} {:answer/id #uuid "fd090184-35cb-509b-9120-0302213fd5c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9 & -16 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a66c93a-af60-53aa-a747-1ca57d557a70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 34 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324193} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a9413c5-a6ce-51cb-995c-4ce6f0f85732" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "196e0a55-17fd-5fa1-bc58-316b9bb71045" :question/math-academy-id "q-38454" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{C}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $C$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $B.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/2e/2e82c232614bec8a98f079ea56d7913ee13e7b457e33e418198278d2e369fc5c.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}.\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{B}.$ Solving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 6}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 34 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129701 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129155 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86028fae-a119-5194-975d-a6d9fad6faf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Given Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1079d3d2-be2f-5cb3-b94c-9018f0762790" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 & -38 \\\\ 8 & -19\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480143} {:answer/id #uuid "4ab2b0d1-3d5f-53f9-8f37-02b8cfded0cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -8 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480239} {:answer/id #uuid "53b397b9-c829-5c9b-b0ea-a550e68d9a00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}19 & -8 \\\\ 38 & -15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480252} {:answer/id #uuid "702184cc-df91-5774-bfc1-66a9113e145d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}19 & 19 \\\\ 38 & 57\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480290} {:answer/id #uuid "7146fe46-6a51-56c2-a398-39cdace60f8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-13 & 9 \\\\ -16 & 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7146fe46-6a51-56c2-a398-39cdace60f8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-13 & 9 \\\\ -16 & 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480294} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd51970d-d30d-5586-b9c7-74ad40f631a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127687}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ba0e0a4a-0049-5942-9e25-8da63ac0f245" :question/math-academy-id "q-38804" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,C=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the bases $B$ and $C$ of ${R}^{2},$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$, shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nFirst, let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ and $\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of vectors from $B$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ relative to the basis $C.$ To do this, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce $M$ using Gaussian elimination until we get the identity matrix on the left. By doing this, we obtain the required change-of-coordinates matrix on the right.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 7\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-3)\\cdot 7-5\\cdot (-4)}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-13 & 9 \\\\ -16 & 11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360747 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "434a82c2-7964-525a-85b9-eb17fa7b5b26" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connections Between Matrices of a Linear Transformation Relative to Different Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62ea197e-9076-5ec7-9c6b-fde342e50e58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452287} {:answer/id #uuid "371eea84-4676-5f33-860c-9ae4e18c7064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "371eea84-4676-5f33-860c-9ae4e18c7064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452288} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3e5c9ca-6cc9-55d4-93e3-da3cb1057919" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452991} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bddeda6b-c779-5d38-b99c-7b9f7c3fd8d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452289} {:answer/id #uuid "e3b2c027-6043-5549-871e-78ddef1107d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bddeda6b-c779-5d38-b99c-7b9f7c3fd8d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452289} :answer-field/id #uuid "51370f87-3ad5-5a80-a161-072ee50a64dd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452992} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de3104b1-f9c6-562b-9198-a923998a0e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452291} {:answer/id #uuid "1fac6913-2157-5d65-b290-ffccbb160d63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de3104b1-f9c6-562b-9198-a923998a0e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452291} :answer-field/id #uuid "e53a4dc2-d964-58e2-b05c-d5768a79a4e5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452993}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "63a8e650-529a-5d09-8a67-87993316a8b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-97061" :question/problem "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $B$ to basis $C,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$\n- **II.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$\n- **III.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360748 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "434a82c2-7964-525a-85b9-eb17fa7b5b26" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connections Between Matrices of a Linear Transformation Relative to Different Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "463ae41e-390b-598e-ad2c-cc70f9b8b51a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452293} {:answer/id #uuid "ca2a9785-fc82-5dbb-91e3-a0ed2dd4ee8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca2a9785-fc82-5dbb-91e3-a0ed2dd4ee8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452294} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc1bf5b2-a5c1-5687-973d-01d75246fa11" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452994} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c91a051-7a46-5af3-abb4-aa9f3ee447ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452295} {:answer/id #uuid "8a857a45-934f-59cb-806a-0ff39125394b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c91a051-7a46-5af3-abb4-aa9f3ee447ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452295} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e95157d-1201-5d7b-96c1-63d2f59338ce" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452995} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82668a3d-f3fe-5542-b38c-eb8caa646e42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452297} {:answer/id #uuid "862c623a-d189-5525-b571-01f6a5171ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "862c623a-d189-5525-b571-01f6a5171ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452298} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a201872-4c57-5d35-8831-ed55fb963e8f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47f484a7-fae0-59b3-b230-0181ae09e78c" :question/math-academy-id "q-97064" :question/problem "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $C$ to basis $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}$\n- **II.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$\n- **III.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/9b/9ba3d1f0eebdfc82c40f36bdbe16896ca15516b623c695b72c331861955329bc.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "434a82c2-7964-525a-85b9-eb17fa7b5b26" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connections Between Matrices of a Linear Transformation Relative to Different Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adfa5bb0-95dd-5e0f-a753-c9aa882957ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452299} {:answer/id #uuid "42f83495-bf79-5e40-bb79-ee3727fa8353" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adfa5bb0-95dd-5e0f-a753-c9aa882957ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452299} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0a51104-0991-584c-8840-d4699e193686" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452997} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc60e2c0-d4d5-572f-9b0e-66723f21b412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452301} {:answer/id #uuid "150625a1-ee19-5f2b-8756-67d6f8188780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "150625a1-ee19-5f2b-8756-67d6f8188780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452302} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9c01461-e833-5fcb-90ac-4d72370339f7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452998} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5af27217-2702-5cd8-b3f6-5240c4009a7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452303} {:answer/id #uuid "f6f2580e-b5b9-544c-bdb5-e0422c549813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6f2580e-b5b9-544c-bdb5-e0422c549813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452304} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae0a334b-94f1-5fb1-ac19-ba3fff9b5671" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452999}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "977acc9f-1a7e-5840-a4f9-507f36de32d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-97065" :question/problem "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $C$ to basis $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}$\n- **II.** $[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}$\n- **III.** $[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/9b/9ba3d1f0eebdfc82c40f36bdbe16896ca15516b623c695b72c331861955329bc.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186480634 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129130 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61bd0b4f-165c-5f31-b4ec-e0eff7e758e1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis Using a Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "477ace4c-82e3-57c5-a4c3-6fc1dcc1600b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480228} {:answer/id #uuid "5fa983bc-fb00-52bc-b27d-c56b5262d607" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}13 & -10 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480270} {:answer/id #uuid "6888f16e-6a85-521f-975e-63342031a0b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480281} {:answer/id #uuid "c9be896a-c20c-55d4-9452-71c1e8bfd917" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480446} {:answer/id #uuid "e57c7b8f-280a-5e63-a865-80fca1154fb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "477ace4c-82e3-57c5-a4c3-6fc1dcc1600b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480228} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bb5b3db-09a2-5068-870b-5e729655be69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "090d811d-2518-5f77-a8e6-7fb33e3ee0bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-97113" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{C}.$ First, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot (-1)-3\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 \\\\ -14 & 11\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395236 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129130 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61bd0b4f-165c-5f31-b4ec-e0eff7e758e1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis Using a Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bd7cba7-4aea-5bfa-ac53-5e6bfef17303" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395238} {:answer/id #uuid "0e9f165b-892b-54a7-ac32-c6ee54ed56fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395239} {:answer/id #uuid "74ebb876-d1f9-5de2-836d-0ce54e1671e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 & -5 \\\\ 26 & -11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395240} {:answer/id #uuid "4d9b8101-9235-5bd1-9d67-397ac4faea30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395241} {:answer/id #uuid "c4818d98-198b-548b-8121-0a8b48614740" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & -7 \\\\ 24 & -17\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e9f165b-892b-54a7-ac32-c6ee54ed56fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395239} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd97dd2b-5eec-58d6-9066-ccafa818ca4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395237}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f59fe0b-284b-5212-bd9c-6b6ffbb22f39" :question/math-academy-id "q-97116" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{C}.$ First, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 5-(-2)\\cdot (-2)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419684 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129131 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "969220db-a686-511b-b33a-0b4f6ab66b1a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b6934d8-eaf0-5f13-b06a-71ac2a0dc0af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419660} {:answer/id #uuid "5c9c3643-ad71-51e0-bd19-40d272c2cabe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419667} {:answer/id #uuid "8f47a664-a9ad-5deb-90c8-17a7a38adab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419671} {:answer/id #uuid "d0704113-7386-54ca-ad0c-7578acd9ac62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -11 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419676} {:answer/id #uuid "dc81c6b4-cc09-56a5-916c-e323cc4197ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c9c3643-ad71-51e0-bd19-40d272c2cabe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419667} :answer-field/id #uuid "32c807d8-09ff-597f-a633-55d26150ec43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "662e0d41-a6b8-58b3-ad4a-e835c48f17e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-97118" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to this basis. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the basis $B$ and standard basis $S$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/db/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360755 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129131 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "969220db-a686-511b-b33a-0b4f6ab66b1a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04ab380b-359f-5fa7-9dd1-5f1f687f5511" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 & 7 \\\\ 8 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357796} {:answer/id #uuid "155b0ef5-ee12-5bbc-9dcb-79ae79e2a845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357940} {:answer/id #uuid "2598bd34-3569-5f50-a023-f6c6e289174b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}17 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358090} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e07147-0972-5a53-bf9f-6b81b9f73133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359442} {:answer/id #uuid "e3f66fb5-a4f6-5e6e-aa7e-7e4c763c1153" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0e07147-0972-5a53-bf9f-6b81b9f73133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359442} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f593899-661f-517f-adb3-211823b247d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "18ca38eb-405c-519d-860c-9cd4de1b59e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-97120" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to this basis. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the basis $B$ and standard basis $S$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/db/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 6}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395243 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129131 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "969220db-a686-511b-b33a-0b4f6ab66b1a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "245cb731-469d-572a-8764-194ea7fe088a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395245} {:answer/id #uuid "f54a6b7e-61b3-5ff8-b9a8-9f20f110085a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 & -8 \\\\ -16 & 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395246} {:answer/id #uuid "398a11ff-8023-5bd5-89f6-9f7aad0aa834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -4 \\\\ -8 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395247} {:answer/id #uuid "59ef0fc5-8743-5c5e-a125-6c5746e60c90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395248} {:answer/id #uuid "4e5b8992-a502-5704-b901-de8d8c4d35b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-13 & -4 \\\\ -7 & -11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "245cb731-469d-572a-8764-194ea7fe088a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :a